# RER Development Workflow

## Before editing

Inspect the files, imports, Server vs Client, and knock-on routes. Change the smallest appropriate surface.

Do not refactor or redesign unrelated code, mass-rename, install packages without reason, delete old implementations during migration, or change backend architecture without approval.

## Dependencies and tests

Prefer the existing stack. If a package is needed, say why and avoid duplicates.

After meaningful work: run the relevant check; run `npm run build` for architectural changes; watch the console; check responsive UI. Compilation alone is not success.

## Git

Never commit, push, force-push, rewrite history, or delete branches unless explicitly instructed.

Before a requested commit, list changed/created/deleted files and build/test status.

## Migration

Keep Vite files until verification. Migrate one area at a time. Do not mix migration with redesign unless asked. Checkpoint after stable phases.

## Documentation

- `docs/PRD.md` — product direction only; edit when requirements actually change.
- `docs/PHASES.md` — roadmap and phase status; update when a phase completes or materially changes.
- `docs/COMPETITORS.md` — competitor research only; no unsupported claims.
- `docs/MEMORY.md` — curated memory. **Do not edit automatically.** If something should persist, report `Potential Memory Update` (see `00-core.mdc`) and wait for approval. Do not log bugfixes, CSS, routine migration progress, or experiments there.
